Attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is a derivative work of vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm),
Copyright the vLLM Team, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

It is a deliberate reimplementation rather than an incidental one: the engine's
control plane -- the scheduler, the KV cache manager and block pool, the request
lifecycle, the OpenAI-compatible HTTP surface -- is ported from vLLM so that a client
cannot tell the two apart, while the device and the model underneath are simulated.
The pinned upstream revision is v0.27.1, recorded with per-file hashes in
vendor/MANIFEST.sha256 and documented in UPSTREAM.md.

Every module states its upstream counterpart and its fidelity tier in its header:

  Tier A  line-for-line with upstream; a behavioural divergence is a bug
  Tier B  signature-faithful, body-thinned
  Tier C  shape-only -- field names, types and validation intent match
  Tier D  invented; no upstream counterpart (pvllm/sim/, pvllm/platforms/sim.py)

Tier A and Tier B modules are the derivative portion. Tier D is original to this
project. `tools/spec_sync.py` checks in CI that every declared counterpart still
exists at the pin, so the attribution above cannot silently go stale.

The vendored copy of upstream under vendor/ is a read-only reference fetched at setup
time. It is not redistributed here: it is excluded by .gitignore, and only its hash
manifest is committed.
